DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       All  rrttnneettlliinnkk(7)  messages  consist of a nneettlliinnkk(7) message header and
       appended attributes.  The attributes should be manipulated  only  using
       the macros provided here.

       RRTTAA__OOKK((_r_t_a,,  _s_i_z_e))  returns  true  if _r_t_a points to a valid routing at‐
       tribute; _s_i_z_e is the running size of the attribute  buffer.   When  not
       true  then you must assume there are no more attributes in the message,
       even if _s_i_z_e is nonzero.

       RRTTAA__DDAATTAA((_r_t_a)) returns a pointer to the start of this attribute’s data.

       RRTTAA__PPAAYYLLOOAADD((_r_t_a)) returns the size of this attribute’s data.

       RRTTAA__NNEEXXTT((_r_t_a,, _s_i_z_e)) gets the next attribute after  _r_t_a.   Calling  this
       macro will update _s_i_z_e.  You should use RRTTAA__OOKK to check the validity of
       the returned pointer.

       RRTTAA__LLEENNGGTTHH((_s_i_z_e))  returns  the size which is required for _s_i_z_e bytes of
       data plus the header.

       RRTTAA__SSPPAACCEE((_s_i_z_e)) returns the amount of space which will be needed  in  a
       message with _s_i_z_e bytes of data.

